Yo, listen up, let me break it down for the crew,
The Fed's the big bank that controls the whole revenue.

They ain't printin' money like a mixtape on the low,
They watch the cash flow, make sure it don't blow.
When the economy's too hype, spendin' too fast,
They raise the interest rate, make the loans a heavier cast.
That cools the party down, stops the price tags from climbin',
Keeps your rent from goin' up, keeps your paper from declinin'.

But if the game gets slow, jobs gettin' scarce,
They drop the rate down, make it easier to invest.
They buy up bonds, pumpin' cash into the street,
So you can get a loan for a new whip or a beat.
They're the DJ of the money, scratchin' the track,
Keepin' the whole economy from a heart attack.

So when you hear "the Fed," don't think it's some fed in a suit,
It's the bank that controls the whole damn loot.
They keep the dollar strong, the game from a crash,
So you can stack your paper and make your money last. [end of text]


